{%- comment -%}
  Product page — port of storefront/src/pages/ProductPage.jsx

  The React PDP was driven by a hardcoded catalog (sizes, colours, a `hookLoop`
  boolean). This one is driven by the store's real variants, which turned out to
  map onto the same three controls exactly:

      option "Size"           -> .pdp__pills
      option "Color"/"Colour" -> .pdp__swatches
      option "Hook or Loop?"  -> .pdp__seg   (Both carries the Recommended flag)

  The "a single side can't fasten on its own" prompt that used to sit under the
  segmented control is gone. The Recommended flag on Both already carries that
  point without interrupting a shopper who knows they only want one side —
  which, for a store selling to trade, is a common and legitimate choice.

  Anything else falls back to pills, so a product with a fourth option still
  renders correctly instead of losing a control.

  Description: React hardcoded PRODUCT_COPY, PRODUCT_DETAILS and their spec
  tables — but that content was scraped from this very store, and product.description
  already carries all of it (description, key features, common applications,
  specifications). Rendering the real field keeps one source of truth and lets
  the merchant edit copy without a deploy. The spec table below it is built from
  data Shopify actually holds (SKU, options, availability), not a second copy.

  Pricing is Shopify's. React computed "both = single x 2" in JS; here Both is a
  real variant with its own price, so the arithmetic disappears.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign product_variant = product.selected_or_first_available_variant
  assign hl_option_index = 0
  for opt in product.options_with_values
    assign nm = opt.name | downcase
    if nm contains 'hook' or nm contains 'loop'
      assign hl_option_index = forloop.index
    endif
  endfor
-%}

<div id="main" class="pdp">
  <div class="wrap pdp__grid">
    <div class="pdp__gallery">
      <div class="pdp__stage" data-hnl-stage>
        <span class="pdp__flag">{{ section.settings.stock_flag }}</span>
        {%- if product.featured_image -%}
          <img src="{{ product.featured_image | image_url: width: 1200 }}"
               alt="{{ product.featured_image.alt | default: product.title | escape }}"
               width="1200" height="1200" data-hnl-main>
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>

      {%- if product.images.size > 1 -%}
        <div class="pdp__thumbs">
          {%- for image in product.images -%}
            <button class="pdp__thumb {% if forloop.first %}is-on{% endif %}"
                    data-hnl-thumb
                    data-image-id="{{ image.id }}"
                    data-full="{{ image | image_url: width: 1200 }}"
                    aria-label="Image {{ forloop.index }}">
              <img src="{{ image | image_url: width: 200 }}" alt="" width="200" height="200" loading="lazy">
            </button>
          {%- endfor -%}
        </div>
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>

    <div class="pdp__buy">
      <span class="pdp__eyebrow">{{ section.settings.eyebrow }}</span>
      <h1 class="pdp__title">{{ product.title }}</h1>
      {%- comment -%}
        Vendor removed from this line. It printed "HOOKNLOOP ·" before the SKU
        while the brand line directly below already names the brand — the same
        fact twice, and the uppercase vendor was the louder of the two despite
        being the less useful. The SKU stands alone here.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <span class="pdp__brand">
        <span class="pdp__brand-sku">SKU <b data-hnl-sku>{{ product_variant.sku }}</b></span>
      </span>

      {%- comment -%}
        Brand line. VELCRO is a registered trademark and a genuine VELCRO Brand
        product is worth more than a generic equivalent — so it is called out
        explicitly rather than left to the title. Detected from the product
        title/type, since product.vendor is "HooknLoop" on every product.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- liquid
        assign is_velcro = false
        assign hay = product.title | append: ' ' | append: product.type | append: ' ' | append: product.tags | downcase
        if hay contains 'velcro' or hay contains 'velcoin'
          assign is_velcro = true
        endif
      -%}
      <span class="pdp__brandline">
        Brand:&nbsp;
        {%- if is_velcro -%}
          {%- comment -%}
            VELCRO® Brand stands alone here. Naming HooknLoop beside it read as
            a co-brand — as though the product were both — when HooknLoop is the
            retailer, not a second maker. The footer trademark note already
            makes that relationship explicit.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          <b class="pdp__brandline-mark">VELCRO&reg;</b>
        {%- else -%}
          <b>HooknLoop</b>
        {%- endif -%}
      </span>

      <div class="pdp__rating">
        {%- comment -%}
          Judge.me is installed on this store; its badge injects into this hook.
          Until a product has reviews it renders nothing, so the fallback below
          keeps the row from collapsing — same as React's "No reviews yet".
        {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- comment -%}
          Judge.me's own markup, copied attribute for attribute from the live
          store, INCLUDING the metafield. Judge.me caches the rendered rating
          and review list into product.metafields.judgeme.*; printing that is
          what puts reviews on the page server-side. An empty placeholder with
          the right classes renders nothing, which is what was happening.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <div class="jdgm-widget jdgm-preview-badge"
             data-id="{{ product.id }}"
             data-template="manual-installation">{{ product.metafields.judgeme.badge }}</div>
        <span class="pdp__rating-none" data-hnl-norating>No reviews yet</span>
      </div>

      <div class="pdp__price">
        <div>
          <span class="pdp__price-now" data-hnl-price>{{ product_variant.price | money }}</span>
          {%- comment -%}
            React qualified the price with "per side" or "complete set" so a
            shopper could tell at a glance whether $32.90 buys a working
            fastener or half of one. Rebuilt from the live option value.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          <span class="pdp__price-unit" data-hnl-price-unit>incl. GST</span>
        </div>
        {%- if product_variant.compare_at_price > product_variant.price -%}
          <s class="pdp__price-was" data-hnl-compare>{{ product_variant.compare_at_price | money }}</s>
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>

      {%- comment -%}
        Liquid's form tag, not a hand-written <form>. That distinction is why the
        Shop Pay button never appeared: {{ form | payment_button }} needs the
        `form` object this tag creates, and a raw <form> leaves it nil, so the
        filter silently rendered nothing. Dynamic checkout was enabled on the
        store the whole time — the live product page renders the button fine.

        The tag also supplies form_type and utf8 itself, so those hidden inputs
        are gone.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- form 'product', product, id: 'hnl-pdp-form', data-hnl-pdp-form: '' -%}
        <input type="hidden" name="id" value="{{ product_variant.id }}" data-hnl-variant-id>

        {%- for option in product.options_with_values -%}
          {%- liquid
            assign oname = option.name | downcase
            assign style = 'pills'
            if oname contains 'colour' or oname contains 'color'
              assign style = 'swatch'
            endif
            if forloop.index == hl_option_index
              assign style = 'seg'
            endif
          -%}

          <div class="pdp__opt" data-hnl-opt data-option-index="{{ forloop.index }}">
            <span class="pdp__opt-label">{{ option.name }} <b data-hnl-opt-value>{{ option.selected_value }}</b></span>

            {%- case style -%}
              {%- when 'swatch' -%}
                <div class="pdp__swatches">
                  {%- for value in option.values -%}
                    <button type="button"
                            class="pdp__swatch {% if value == option.selected_value %}is-on{% endif %}"
                            data-hnl-val="{{ value | escape }}"
                            aria-label="{{ value | escape }}"
                            style="background: {% render 'hnl-swatch-fill', value: value %}"></button>
                  {%- endfor -%}
                </div>

              {%- when 'seg' -%}
                <div class="pdp__seg" role="radiogroup" aria-label="Choose {{ option.name | downcase }}">
                  {%- comment -%}
                    "Both" still leads, because a single side cannot fasten to
                    anything on its own, but it no longer carries a Recommended
                    badge — the store sells all three as equal choices and the
                    flag was steering the pick.
                  {%- endcomment -%}
                  {%- for value in option.values -%}
                    {%- assign v = value | downcase -%}
                    {%- if v == 'both' -%}
                      <button type="button" class="pdp__seg-btn {% if value == option.selected_value %}is-on{% endif %}"
                              role="radio" aria-checked="{% if value == option.selected_value %}true{% else %}false{% endif %}"
                              data-hnl-val="{{ value | escape }}">
                        <span class="pdp__seg-t">Both</span>
                        <span class="pdp__seg-s">Complete set</span>
                      </button>
                    {%- endif -%}
                  {%- endfor -%}
                  {%- for value in option.values -%}
                    {%- assign v = value | downcase -%}
                    {%- unless v == 'both' -%}
                      {%- comment -%}
                        "Look" is a typo for "Loop" in the option values on
                        Fire Retardant Adhesive. Corrected on screen only —
                        data-hnl-val keeps the real value, because that is what
                        the variant lookup matches on and what Shopify expects
                        back at add-to-cart. Fixing the option value in admin
                        would retire this branch.
                      {%- endcomment -%}
                      <button type="button" class="pdp__seg-btn {% if value == option.selected_value %}is-on{% endif %}"
                              role="radio" aria-checked="{% if value == option.selected_value %}true{% else %}false{% endif %}"
                              data-hnl-val="{{ value | escape }}">
                        <span class="pdp__seg-t">{% if v == 'look' %}Loop{% else %}{{ value }}{% endif %}</span>
                        <span class="pdp__seg-s">{% if v == 'hook' %}Stiff side{% elsif v == 'loop' or v == 'look' %}Soft side{% endif %}</span>
                      </button>
                    {%- endunless -%}
                  {%- endfor -%}
                </div>


              {%- else -%}
                <div class="pdp__pills">
                  {%- for value in option.values -%}
                    <button type="button" class="pdp__pill {% if value == option.selected_value %}is-on{% endif %}"
                            data-hnl-val="{{ value | escape }}">{{ value }}</button>
                  {%- endfor -%}
                </div>
            {%- endcase -%}
          </div>
        {%- endfor -%}

        <div class="pdp__cta">
          <div class="pdp__cta-row">
            <div class="pdp__qty" role="group" aria-label="Quantity">
              <button type="button" data-hnl-qty="-1" aria-label="Decrease quantity">&minus;</button>
              <span aria-live="polite" data-hnl-qty-val>1</span>
              <button type="button" data-hnl-qty="1" aria-label="Increase quantity">+</button>
            </div>
            <input type="hidden" name="quantity" value="1" data-hnl-qty-input>
            <button type="submit" class="btn btn--primary pdp__add" data-hnl-add
                    {% unless product_variant.available %}disabled{% endunless %}>
              <span data-hnl-add-label>
                {%- if product_variant.available -%}
                  Add to cart &mdash; <span data-hnl-total>{{ product_variant.price | money }}</span>
                {%- else -%}
                  Sold out
                {%- endif -%}
              </span>
            </button>
            {%- comment -%}
              The add now happens without a page load, so nothing announces it.
              This says so once, for screen readers only.
            {%- endcomment -%}
            {%- comment -%}
              Volume saving for the quantity currently chosen, filled by
              applyBulk(). Starts hidden so it never flashes an empty row
              before the first render.
            {%- endcomment -%}
            <p class="pdp__bulknote" data-hnl-bulk-note hidden></p>
            <p id="hnl-cart-live" class="visually-hidden" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p>
          </div>

          {%- comment -%}
            Shopify's own accelerated checkout — Shop Pay and whatever else this
            store has enabled. React faked this with a styled button; the real
            one actually completes a purchase.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          {{ form | payment_button }}
        </div>
      {%- endform -%}

      <div class="pdp__policies">
        <a href="/pages/shipping-delivery"><span class="pdp__tico"><svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.9" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M2 6h11v11H2zM13 9h4l3 3v5h-7"/><circle cx="6" cy="18" r="1.6"/><circle cx="17" cy="18" r="1.6"/></svg></span>Shipping</a>
        <a href="/pages/return-policy"><span class="pdp__tico"><svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.9" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M3 12a9 9 0 1 0 3-6.7L3 8m0-5v5h5"/></svg></span>Returns &amp; Exchanges</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  {%- comment -%} Buy More & Save — the live store's volume ladder. {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- if section.settings.show_bulk -%}
    <section class="pdp__bulk" aria-labelledby="bms-h">
      <div class="wrap">
        <div class="bms">
          <div class="bms__top">
            <span class="bms__eyebrow">{{ section.settings.bulk_eyebrow }}</span>
            <h2 id="bms-h" class="bms__h">{{ section.settings.bulk_heading }}</h2>
            <p class="bms__sub">{{ section.settings.bulk_sub }}</p>
          </div>
          {%- comment -%}
            data-min / data-pct are what let the buy box price itself against
            these tiers as the quantity changes, and what lets the matching
            card light up. Parsed from the same strings the panel prints, so
            editing a tier in the theme editor moves both together — there is
            no second copy of the numbers to fall out of sync.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          <div class="bms__tiers" data-hnl-tiers>
            {%- assign tiers = section.settings.bulk_tiers | newline_to_br | split: '<br />' -%}
            {%- for tier in tiers -%}
              {%- assign bits = tier | strip | split: '|' -%}
              {%- if bits.size >= 2 -%}
                {%- assign tmin = bits[0] | strip | replace: 'Buy ', '' | replace: '+', '' | replace: ' rolls', '' | strip -%}
                {%- assign tpct = bits[1] | strip | replace: '%', '' | strip -%}
                <div class="bms__tier {% if forloop.last %}is-best{% endif %}"
                     style="--i: {{ forloop.index0 }}"
                     data-min="{{ tmin }}" data-pct="{{ tpct }}">
                  {%- if forloop.last -%}<span class="bms__ribbon">Best value</span>{%- endif -%}
                  <span class="bms__qty">{{ bits[0] | strip }}</span>
                  <span class="bms__pct">{{ bits[1] | strip }}</span>
                  <span class="bms__lbl">off</span>
                </div>
              {%- endif -%}
            {%- endfor -%}
          </div>
        </div>

        <ul class="bms__trust">
          <li><span class="bms__tico"><svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.9" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M2 6h11v11H2zM13 9h4l3 3v5h-7"/><circle cx="6" cy="18" r="1.6"/><circle cx="17" cy="18" r="1.6"/></svg></span><span class="bms__tcopy"><b>Fast Australian shipping</b><em>Speedy delivery Australia-wide</em></span></li>
          <li><span class="bms__tico"><svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.9" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><rect x="4.5" y="10.5" width="15" height="10" rx="2"/><path d="M8 10.5V7a4 4 0 0 1 8 0v3.5"/></svg></span><span class="bms__tcopy"><b>Secured payment</b><em>Safe checkout with SSL encryption</em></span></li>
          <li><span class="bms__tico"><svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.9" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M3 12a9 9 0 1 0 3-6.7L3 8m0-5v5h5"/></svg></span><span class="bms__tcopy"><b>Easy returns</b><em>{{ section.settings.returns_note }}</em></span></li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>
  {%- endif -%}

  <div class="pdp__lower">
    <div class="wrap pdp__cols pdp__cols--single">
      <div class="pdp__main-col">
        <section class="pdp__block">
          <h2>Specifications</h2>
          <table class="pdp__spec">
            <tbody>
              <tr><th>Brand</th><td>{{ product.vendor | default: shop.name }}</td></tr>
              <tr><th>SKU</th><td data-hnl-sku>{{ product_variant.sku }}</td></tr>
              {%- for option in product.options_with_values -%}
                <tr><th>{{ option.name }}</th><td>{{ option.values | join: ', ' }}</td></tr>
              {%- endfor -%}
              {%- if product.type != blank -%}<tr><th>Type</th><td>{{ product.type }}</td></tr>{%- endif -%}
              <tr><th>Availability</th><td data-hnl-avail>{% if product_variant.available %}In stock{% else %}Out of stock{% endif %}</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
          <p class="pdp__spec-note">{{ section.settings.spec_note }}</p>
        </section>

        {%- if product.description != blank -%}
          <section class="pdp__block">
            <h2>Description</h2>
            <div class="pdp__rte">{% render 'hnl-copy-rules', html: product.description, handle: product.handle %}</div>
            {%- comment -%}
              In-use photography sits with the description's own "Common
              Applications" copy rather than in a section of its own — see the
              note in the snippet.

              Specifications now precedes this block. With Description first,
              the photos landed directly above the "Specifications" heading and
              read as though they illustrated the spec table. Ending the block
              with them, followed by the FAQs, keeps them attached to the
              applications copy they belong to.
            {%- endcomment -%}
            {% render 'hnl-product-applications', product: product %}
          </section>
        {%- endif -%}


        {%- comment -%}
          The store's real FAQs, per product. Section blocks below act as a
          fallback for a product that has none of its own — empty by default,
          because the live store shows nothing for those four products and
          borrowing another product's answers would put words in its mouth.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- capture product_faqs -%}{% render 'hnl-product-faqs', product: product %}{%- endcapture -%}
        {%- if product_faqs contains 'pdp__faq-item' -%}
          {{ product_faqs }}
        {%- elsif section.blocks.size > 0 -%}
          <section class="pdp__block">
            <h2>Questions, answered</h2>
            <div class="pdp__faq">
              {%- for block in section.blocks -%}
                {%- if block.type == 'faq' -%}
                  <div class="pdp__faq-item {% if forloop.first %}is-open{% endif %}" {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
                    <button type="button" data-hnl-faq aria-expanded="{% if forloop.first %}true{% else %}false{% endif %}">
                      {{ block.settings.q }}<span aria-hidden="true">{% if forloop.first %}&minus;{% else %}+{% endif %}</span>
                    </button>
                    <p {% unless forloop.first %}hidden{% endunless %}>{{ block.settings.a }}</p>
                  </div>
                {%- endif -%}
              {%- endfor -%}
            </div>
          </section>
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- comment -%}
          The full review list and the "Write a review" button. Judge.me looks
          for id="judgeme_product_reviews" specifically, and needs the product
          id and title to load reviews and to attribute a new one — an anchor
          named "reviews" with only data-id rendered nothing at all.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- comment -%}
          Reviews. On this store Judge.me's review widget is an APP BLOCK, not a
          manual div — the live page renders it inside a shopify-app-block with
          a data-block-id and its own entry point. A hand-written
          .jdgm-review-widget has nothing to attach to, which is why the list
          and the "Write a review" button never appeared.

          The section accepts @app blocks now, so Judge.me (or any review app)
          drops in here from the theme editor. The manual div is kept as a
          fallback for when no app block has been added, so the anchor is never
          empty.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <div id="reviews" class="pdp__reviews">
          {%- assign has_app_block = false -%}
          {%- for block in section.blocks -%}
            {%- if block.type == '@app' -%}{%- assign has_app_block = true -%}{%- endif -%}
          {%- endfor -%}

          {%- if has_app_block -%}
            {%- for block in section.blocks -%}
              {%- if block.type == '@app' -%}
                {% render block %}
              {%- endif -%}
            {%- endfor -%}
          {%- else -%}
            <div id="judgeme_product_reviews"
                 class="jdgm-widget jdgm-review-widget"
                 data-product-title="{{ product.title | escape }}"
                 data-id="{{ product.id }}"
                 data-product-id="{{ product.id }}">{{ product.metafields.judgeme.widget }}</div>
          {%- endif -%}
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    {%- assign related = collections[section.settings.related_collection].products | default: collections.all.products -%}
    {%- if related.size > 1 -%}
      <div class="wrap pdp__related">
        <div class="pdp__related-head">
          <h2>Related products</h2>
          <a href="{{ routes.all_products_collection_url }}" class="pdp__related-all">Shop all products &rarr;</a>
        </div>
        <div class="pdp__related-grid">
          {%- assign shown = 0 -%}
          {%- for item in related -%}
            {%- if item.handle != product.handle and shown < 4 -%}
              {%- assign shown = shown | plus: 1 -%}
              {% render 'hnl-product-card', product: item %}
            {%- endif -%}
          {%- endfor -%}
        </div>
      </div>
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>

  {%- comment -%}
    Sticky dock. Submits the same form above via its form attribute, so there is
    exactly one source of truth for the selected variant and quantity.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <div class="pdp__dock" data-hnl-dock role="region" aria-label="Add to cart">
    <div class="pdp__dock-inner">
      <div class="pdp__dock-info">
        <span class="pdp__dock-thumb">
          {%- if product.featured_image -%}
            <img src="{{ product.featured_image | image_url: width: 160 }}" alt="" width="160" height="160" loading="lazy">
          {%- endif -%}
        </span>
        <span class="pdp__dock-meta">
          <b class="pdp__dock-name">{{ product.title }}</b>
          <span class="pdp__dock-variant" data-hnl-dock-variant>{{ product_variant.title }}</span>
          <span class="pdp__dock-mprice"><b data-hnl-total>{{ product_variant.price | money }}</b> incl. GST</span>
        </span>
      </div>

      <div class="pdp__dock-actions">
        <span class="pdp__dock-price"><b data-hnl-total>{{ product_variant.price | money }}</b><em>incl. GST</em></span>
        <div class="pdp__dock-qty" role="group" aria-label="Quantity">
          <button type="button" data-hnl-qty="-1" aria-label="Decrease quantity">&minus;</button>
          <span aria-live="polite" data-hnl-qty-val>1</span>
          <button type="button" data-hnl-qty="1" aria-label="Increase quantity">+</button>
        </div>
        <button type="submit" form="hnl-pdp-form" class="btn btn--primary pdp__dock-add" data-hnl-add
                {% unless product_variant.available %}disabled{% endunless %}>
          <svg class="pdp__dock-cart" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M6 6h15l-1.5 9h-12z"/><circle cx="9" cy="20" r="1.4"/><circle cx="18" cy="20" r="1.4"/><path d="M6 6 5 3H2"/></svg>Add to cart
        </button>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<script type="application/json" data-hnl-variants>
  {{ product.variants | json }}
</script>

<script>
(function () {
  var root = document.querySelector('.pdp');
  if (!root) return;

  var form     = root.querySelector('[data-hnl-pdp-form]');
  var variants = JSON.parse(root.parentNode.querySelector('[data-hnl-variants]')
                 ? root.parentNode.querySelector('[data-hnl-variants]').textContent
                 : document.querySelector('[data-hnl-variants]').textContent);
  var optGroups = [].slice.call(root.querySelectorAll('[data-hnl-opt]'));
  var qty = 1;
  var userPicked = false;   /* has the shopper touched an option control yet? */

  var money = function (cents) {
    return '$' + (cents / 100).toFixed(2);
  };

  function selected() {
    return optGroups.map(function (g) {
      var on = g.querySelector('.is-on');
      return on ? on.getAttribute('data-hnl-val') : null;
    });
  }

  function findVariant(opts) {
    for (var i = 0; i < variants.length; i++) {
      var v = variants[i], ok = true;
      for (var j = 0; j < opts.length; j++) {
        if (opts[j] !== null && v.options[j] !== opts[j]) { ok = false; break; }
      }
      if (ok) return v;
    }
    return null;
  }

  function setAll(sel, fn) {
    [].forEach.call(root.querySelectorAll(sel), fn);
  }

  function render() {
    var opts = selected();
    var v = findVariant(opts);

    /* Update every label to the value actually chosen. */
    optGroups.forEach(function (g) {
      var on = g.querySelector('.is-on');
      var lbl = g.querySelector('[data-hnl-opt-value]');
      if (on && lbl) lbl.textContent = on.getAttribute('data-hnl-val');
      [].forEach.call(g.querySelectorAll('[role="radio"]'), function (b) {
        b.setAttribute('aria-checked', b.classList.contains('is-on') ? 'true' : 'false');
      });
    });

    if (!v) return;

    root.querySelector('[data-hnl-variant-id]').value = v.id;
    setAll('[data-hnl-sku]', function (e) { e.textContent = v.sku || '—'; });
    setAll('[data-hnl-avail]', function (e) { e.textContent = v.available ? 'In stock' : 'Out of stock'; });
    setAll('[data-hnl-total]', function (e) { e.textContent = money(v.price * qty); });

    var price = root.querySelector('[data-hnl-price]');
    if (price) price.textContent = money(v.price);

    var dockVar = root.querySelector('[data-hnl-dock-variant]');
    if (dockVar) dockVar.textContent = v.title;

    syncVariantImage(v);

    setAll('[data-hnl-add]', function (b) {
      b.disabled = !v.available;
      var lbl = b.querySelector('[data-hnl-add-label]');
      /* While the button is showing the green "View cart" confirmation, leave
         its label alone — a price re-render here would silently wipe it. */
      if (lbl && !added) {
        lbl.innerHTML = v.available
          ? 'Add to cart &mdash; <span data-hnl-total>' + money(v.price * qty) + '</span>'
          : 'Sold out';
      }
    });

    /* Put the variant in the URL only once the shopper has actually chosen one.
       Writing it on first paint rewrote a clean /products/<handle> into
       ?variant=… before anyone had touched a control — which made every share,
       copy or bookmark of a product page carry a variant nobody picked. Now the
       URL stays clean until a size, colour or side is selected, and from then on
       it tracks the selection so a shared link opens on the same variant. */
    /* After the label rewrite above, which recreates the total span with the
       undiscounted figure — this is what puts the tier price back. */
    applyBulk(v);

    if (userPicked && history.replaceState) {
      var u = new URL(window.location.href);
      u.searchParams.set('variant', v.id);
      history.replaceState({}, '', u);
    }

  }

  /* Add to cart — stay on the page, then offer the cart.

     The form still POSTs natively without JS, so the no-script path keeps
     working; this only upgrades it. On success both buttons (inline and the
     sticky dock) turn green and read "View cart", and the next click goes to
     the cart instead of adding a second one — which is the mistake the old
     behaviour invited, since it navigated away and people came back and
     clicked again.

     Picking a different size, colour or side resets them: at that point the
     shopper is looking at a variant they have not added, so a green "View
     cart" would be lying about what is in the basket. */
  {%- comment -%}
    Volume pricing, shown while the shopper is still choosing.

    The four tiers are real automatic discounts in Shopify (verified: 5+ =5%,
    10+ =10%, 20+ =20%, 50+ =30%, all active), and they did apply — but only
    at the cart, so raising the quantity here changed nothing on screen and
    the "Buy more & save" panel below read as decoration. Someone typing 10
    had no reason to believe the promise until two pages later.

    Tiers are read from the panel's own data attributes, so the numbers cannot
    drift apart.

    Called an estimate deliberately. Shopify applies these across the whole
    order, so a shopper with five of two products also qualifies — this box
    can only speak for the line in front of it, and the cart remains the
    authority.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  var tierEls = [].slice.call(root.querySelectorAll('[data-hnl-tiers] .bms__tier'));
  var tiers = tierEls.map(function (el) {
    return { el: el,
             min: parseInt(el.getAttribute('data-min'), 10) || 0,
             pct: parseFloat(el.getAttribute('data-pct')) || 0 };
  }).filter(function (t) { return t.min > 0 && t.pct > 0; })
    .sort(function (a, b) { return a.min - b.min; });

  function tierFor(n) {
    var hit = null;
    tiers.forEach(function (t) { if (n >= t.min) hit = t; });
    return hit;
  }

  function applyBulk(v) {
    var t = tierFor(qty);
    var full = v.price * qty;
    var now = t ? Math.round(full * (1 - t.pct / 100)) : full;

    tiers.forEach(function (x) { x.el.classList.toggle('is-active', !!t && x.min === t.min); });

    setAll('[data-hnl-total]', function (e) { e.textContent = money(now); });

    var note = root.querySelector('[data-hnl-bulk-note]');
    if (note) {
      if (t) {
        note.innerHTML = '<b>' + t.pct + '% off</b> at ' + qty + ' &mdash; you save '
                       + money(full - now) + ' <span>applied at checkout</span>';
        note.hidden = false;
      } else if (tiers.length) {
        var next = tiers[0];
        note.innerHTML = 'Add ' + (next.min - qty) + ' more for <b>' + next.pct + '% off</b>';
        note.hidden = false;
      } else {
        note.hidden = true;
      }
    }
    return now;
  }

  /* The confirmation is a flash, not a mode: green "Added to cart" for a beat,
     then straight back to "Add to cart". It used to latch into a "View cart"
     button, which meant the primary action on the page stopped being "add" —
     and the drawer that opens alongside already offers the cart and checkout,
     so the button never needed to carry that job. */
  var added = false;
  var addedTimer = null;
  var ADDED_MS = 2200;

  function setAdded(on) {
    added = on;
    setAll('[data-hnl-add]', function (b) {
      b.classList.toggle('is-added', on);
      var lbl = b.querySelector('[data-hnl-add-label]');
      if (on) {
        if (!b.hasAttribute('data-hnl-add-restore') && lbl) {
          b.setAttribute('data-hnl-add-restore', lbl.innerHTML);
        }
        if (lbl) lbl.innerHTML = '&#10003; Added to cart';
        else b.innerHTML = '&#10003; Added to cart';
      } else if (b.hasAttribute('data-hnl-add-restore')) {
        if (lbl) lbl.innerHTML = b.getAttribute('data-hnl-add-restore');
        b.removeAttribute('data-hnl-add-restore');
      }
    });

    clearTimeout(addedTimer);
    if (on) {
      var live = document.getElementById('hnl-cart-live');
      if (live) live.textContent = 'Added to cart.';
      /* Re-render after reverting so the label picks up the current variant
         price, in case the shopper changed quantity while it was green. */
      addedTimer = setTimeout(function () { setAdded(false); render(); }, ADDED_MS);
    }
  }

  if (form) {
    form.addEventListener('submit', function (e) {
      /* Second press: honour the label and go to the cart. */
      /* No special case while the confirmation is showing — pressing again
         adds another one, which is what a button reading "Add to cart" should
         do. The drawer is where the cart and checkout live. */
      if (!window.fetch) return;                 /* let the browser post it */
      e.preventDefault();

      {%- comment -%}
        This used to run three round trips before anything happened —
        /cart/add.js, then /cart.js for the badge, then the drawer's own
        /cart.js — with every add button disabled for the whole sequence. That
        is why it felt like the press did nothing.

        The confirmation is now shown on the press itself, before the network
        is touched, and the redundant /cart.js is gone: the drawer already
        updates the header badge when it renders. Two round trips became one,
        and the feedback is immediate.

        Buttons are no longer disabled. The green state is the feedback, and
        disabling was what made a slow connection feel broken.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      setAdded(true);

      fetch('/cart/add.js', {
        method: 'POST',
        body: new FormData(form),
        headers: { 'Accept': 'application/json' },
        credentials: 'same-origin'
      })
        .then(function (r) { return r.ok ? r.json() : r.json().then(function (j) { throw new Error(j.description || 'Could not add to cart'); }); })
        .then(function () {
          /* The drawer reads /cart.js itself and refreshes the badge from the
             same payload, so the two cannot disagree. */
          document.dispatchEvent(new CustomEvent('hnl:cart:open'));
        })
        .catch(function (err) {
          /* Never strand the shopper: undo the optimistic confirmation and
             fall back to a real form post. */
          setAdded(false);
          console.warn('[hnl] add to cart failed, posting form', err);
          form.submit();
        });
    });
  }

  /* Option buttons */
  optGroups.forEach(function (g) {
    g.addEventListener('click', function (e) {
      var btn = e.target.closest('[data-hnl-val]');
      if (!btn) return;
      [].forEach.call(g.querySelectorAll('[data-hnl-val]'), function (b) { b.classList.remove('is-on'); });
      btn.classList.add('is-on');
      userPicked = true;
      if (added) setAdded(false);
      render();
    });
  });

  /* Quantity — the two steppers (inline and dock) stay in lockstep. */
  setAll('[data-hnl-qty]', function (b) {
    b.addEventListener('click', function () {
      qty = Math.max(1, qty + parseInt(b.getAttribute('data-hnl-qty'), 10));
      setAll('[data-hnl-qty-val]', function (e) { e.textContent = qty; });
      root.querySelector('[data-hnl-qty-input]').value = qty;
      render();
    });
  });

  /* Gallery: the shopper clicks a thumb, or picks a colour. */
  var main = root.querySelector('[data-hnl-main]');
  var thumbs = [].slice.call(root.querySelectorAll('[data-hnl-thumb]'));
  var gi = 0, touched = false;

  function showImage(n) {
    if (!thumbs[n] || !main) return;
    gi = n;
    main.src = thumbs[n].getAttribute('data-full');
    thumbs.forEach(function (t, k) { t.classList.toggle('is-on', k === n); });
  }

  thumbs.forEach(function (t, n) {
    t.addEventListener('click', function () { touched = true; showImage(n); });
  });

  /* Picking Black or White should show that colour. Shopify assigns an image
     per variant, so the variant's own featured_image is the source of truth —
     matched to a thumb by image id rather than by URL, because the thumb URL is
     a resized derivative and would never compare equal to the variant's.

     Variants without their own image leave the gallery alone: on a product
     photographed once, changing size or hook/loop should not reset what the
     shopper is looking at. */
  function syncVariantImage(v) {
    if (!v || !v.featured_image || !main) return;
    var id = String(v.featured_image.id);
    for (var i = 0; i < thumbs.length; i++) {
      if (thumbs[i].getAttribute('data-image-id') === id) { showImage(i); return; }
    }
  }

  /* The gallery used to auto-advance every 3.5s until the shopper clicked a
     thumb. Removed: on a product page the image is something you study, and
     swapping it out from under someone mid-look is the opposite of helpful —
     it also fought the variant sync below, which changes the image on purpose.
     The image now only ever changes when the shopper asks it to, by clicking a
     thumb or picking a colour. */

  /* FAQ accordion */
  setAll('[data-hnl-faq]', function (b) {
    b.addEventListener('click', function () {
      var item = b.parentNode;
      var open = item.classList.toggle('is-open');
      b.setAttribute('aria-expanded', open ? 'true' : 'false');
      b.querySelector('span').textContent = open ? '−' : '+';
      var p = item.querySelector('p');
      if (p) p.hidden = !open;
    });
  });

  /* Dock rides between the real CTA and the footer, never over either. */
  var dock = root.querySelector('[data-hnl-dock]');
  var cta = root.querySelector('.pdp__cta');
  var footer = document.querySelector('.ft') || document.querySelector('footer');
  var pastCta = false, atFooter = false;

  function syncDock() {
    var show = pastCta && !atFooter;
    dock.classList.toggle('is-shown', show);
    /* Tell the floating call/chat buttons to stand down on mobile, where the
       dock would otherwise land on top of them. */
    document.body.classList.toggle('dock-open', show);
  }

  if ('IntersectionObserver' in window && cta) {
    new IntersectionObserver(function (en) {
      pastCta = en[0].boundingClientRect.top < 0;
      syncDock();
    }, { threshold: 0 }).observe(cta);

    if (footer) {
      new IntersectionObserver(function (en) {
        atFooter = en[0].isIntersecting;
        syncDock();
      }, { threshold: 0.05 }).observe(footer);
    }
  }

  /* Hide the "No reviews yet" fallback once Judge.me paints a real badge. */
  var none = root.querySelector('[data-hnl-norating]');
  var badge = root.querySelector('.jdgm-preview-badge');
  if (none && badge && 'MutationObserver' in window) {
    new MutationObserver(function () {
      if (badge.textContent.trim()) none.style.display = 'none';
    }).observe(badge, { childList: true, subtree: true });
  }

  render();
})();
</script>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "HooknLoop product",
  "tag": "section",
  "settings": [
    { "type": "text", "id": "eyebrow", "label": "Eyebrow", "default": "Australian stock · fast dispatch" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "stock_flag", "label": "Gallery flag", "default": "In stock · ships in 1–2 days" },
    { "type": "collection", "id": "related_collection", "label": "Related products from", "info": "Defaults to all products." },
    { "type": "textarea", "id": "spec_note", "label": "Specifications note", "default": "Specifications are from the manufacturer's data. Fire-retardant standards are on the supplier's technical data sheet, supplied on request — we don't publish a rating we can't certify." },

    { "type": "header", "content": "Buy more & save" },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "show_bulk", "label": "Show the volume ladder", "default": true },
    { "type": "text", "id": "bulk_eyebrow", "label": "Eyebrow", "default": "Trade & bulk pricing" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "bulk_heading", "label": "Heading", "default": "Buy more & save" },
    { "type": "textarea", "id": "bulk_sub", "label": "Subheading", "default": "The more you order, the less you pay — volume discounts apply automatically at checkout, no code needed." },
    { "type": "textarea", "id": "bulk_tiers", "label": "Tiers", "info": "One per line: Quantity | Discount. Set the matching discounts in Shopify Discounts — this table only displays them.", "default": "Buy 5+ | 5%\nBuy 10+ | 10%\nBuy 20+ | 20%\nBuy 50+ | 30%" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "returns_note", "label": "Returns note", "default": "14-day returns policy" }
  ],
  "blocks": [
    { "type": "@app" },
    {
      "type": "faq",
      "name": "FAQ",
      "settings": [
        { "type": "text", "id": "q", "label": "Question" },
        { "type": "textarea", "id": "a", "label": "Answer" }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "max_blocks": 12
}
{% endschema %}
